description:
Q.7b (bd babelstone-2t16.10) flipped CodeQL's codeql-failon.sh to blocking, but discovered that the 35 Security-tab alerts it was framed around are actually grype SBOM-scan findings (sbom.yml), NOT CodeQL findings — codeql-failon.sh only evaluates CodeQL's own SARIF. So the grype SCA backlog is still UNGATED (sbom.yml ships fail-build: false, report-only).

All 35 were triaged as grype CPE false positives (matches the .NET framework ASSEMBLY version 10.0.0.0 against advisory PACKAGE ranges; authoritative 'dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive' is CLEAN; pinned SDK 10.0.300 resolves runtime 10.0.8, above all fixed versions) and DISMISSED in the Security tab under Q.7b.

To actually gate the SCA leg without those false positives re-blocking:
(1) add a .grype.yaml 'ignore:' config suppressing the .NET framework-assembly CPE false positives (by GHSA/CVE id + package, scoped narrowly) so they do not reappear or block;
(2) flip sbom.yml's anchore/scan-action fail-build: false -> true (severity-cutoff stays high);
(3) decide whether the SBOM job joins the ADR-PC-019 §P1 required-check set (add an always-run gate like CodeQL/CI, or fold into an existing gate) — sbom.yml currently has no aggregator gate job;
(4) confirm a genuinely-vulnerable dependency (seeded) blocks, while the suppressed framework-assembly CPEs do not.

Context: sbom.yml lines 82-88 already anticipate this ('Flipping to fail-build: true is gated on (a) triaging this baseline to zero/suppressing CPE false positives and (b) wiring it into the §P1 required-check set'). ADR-IC-014's SCA leg is Dependabot; the grype SBOM scan is a Q.4 (bd babelstone-2t16.9) addition, so confirm this gating is consistent with ADR-IC-014 §Decision or amend it.

ADR-PC-010 Open Action #3 — the MECHANICAL half of MONEY_BOUNDARY_FIXTURES (catalogue #2 is 'unit + analyser'; B.1/archie-s8gn delivered the unit half). A Microsoft.CodeAnalysis (Roslyn) DiagnosticAnalyzer project + analyzer tests that:
- ban raw Math.Round(decimal, …) anywhere outside Money.FromCents (the single rounding boundary, §P2);
- ban decimal fields/properties outside the Babelstone.Money namespace (§P1);
- flag operator overloads that return decimal from Money inputs.
Wire as an analyzer PackageReference/ProjectReference so it runs in dotnet build + CI with warnings-as-errors. Depends on B.1 (Money type exists). Anchors: ADR-PC-010 §P1–§P2, Open Action #3.
